    "Description": "A transparency slide showing a detail of the left side of a carousel pig head. Some of the pig has red paint on it, and some of the pig has had the paint stripped from it. The pig has tusks on the bottom jaw that are visible. The slide has printed at the top “PULLEN PARK CAROUSEL PULLEN PARK” as well as handwritten “16A’ and “Restricted use left Head”. The bottom has written “Pig” and “6-79” and has typed “RALEIGH NC WAKE CO RR RALEIGH FINE ARTS SOCIETY”.",
